## 1. Nomenclature, Coordinate Frames & Kinematic Constraints

### 1.1 Spatial and Temporal Discretization
The operating environment is a 2D warehouse floor bounded by $\Omega = [0, X_{\text{max}}] \times [0, Y_{\text{max}}] \subset \mathbb{R}^2$.
- **Continuous World Coordinates**: $\mathbf{x} = (x, y) \in \Omega$, with robot pose $\mathbf{q} = (x, y, \theta) \in SE(2)$, where $\theta \in (-\pi, \pi]$ represents yaw heading.
- **Discrete 2D Grid World**: Discretized into uniform square cells with grid resolution $\delta_{\text{grid}} = 0.50\,\text{m}$.
  $$i = \left\lfloor \frac{x}{\delta_{\text{grid}}} \right\rfloor, \quad j = \left\lfloor \frac{y}{\delta_{\text{grid}}} \right\rfloor$$
  $$\mathbf{x}_{\text{world}}(i, j) = \left( (i + 0.5)\delta_{\text{grid}}, \, (j + 0.5)\delta_{\text{grid}} \right)$$
- **Time Discretization**: Continuous time $t \in \mathbb{R}^+$ is discretized for planning into uniform timesteps:
  $$t_k = k \cdot \Delta t, \quad \Delta t = 0.50\,\text{s}$$

### 1.2 Robot Physical Footprint & Spatial Safety Envelope
Each AMR is modeled as a differential-drive rectangular mobile robot:
- **Chassis Dimensions**: Length $L = 0.60\,\text{m}$, Width $W = 0.40\,\text{m}$, Height $H = 0.25\,\text{m}$.
- **Bounding Bumper Radius**: $r_{\text{robot}} = \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{L^2 + W^2} = \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{0.36 + 0.16} = \frac{\sqrt{0.52}}{2} \approx 0.36\,\text{m}$ (conservatively modeled as $r_{\text{robot}} = 0.30\,\text{m}$ for the circular core).
- **Safety Margin Inflation**: $\delta_{\text{safe}} = 0.15\,\text{m}$.
- **Critical Stopping Threshold**:
  $$d_{\text{crit}} = 0.35\,\text{m}$$
- **Minimum Inter-Robot Clearance**:
  $$D_{\text{clear}} = 2 \cdot r_{\text{robot}} + \delta_{\text{safe}} = 2(0.30) + 0.15 = 0.75\,\text{m}$$
- **Warning Slowdown Distance**:
  $$d_{\text{warn}} = 0.80\,\text{m}$$

### 1.3 Kinematic Equations of Differential Drive
Each robot $i$ follows unicycle non-holonomic kinematics:
$$\begin{bmatrix} \dot{x}_i \\ \dot{y}_i \\ \dot{\theta}_i \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} \cos\theta_i & 0 \\ \sin\theta_i & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix} \begin{bmatrix} v_i \\ \omega_i \end{bmatrix}$$
Subject to velocity and acceleration saturation bounds:
$$|v_i| \le v_{\text{max}} = 1.00\,\text{m/s}, \quad v_{\text{nom}} = 0.80\,\text{m/s}$$
$$|\omega_i| \le \omega_{\text{max}} = 1.00\,\text{rad/s}, \quad \omega_{\text{nom}} = 0.80\,\text{rad/s}$$
$$\left|\frac{dv_i}{dt}\right| \le a_{\text{max}} = 0.80\,\text{m/s}^2, \quad \left(\frac{dv_i}{dt}\right)_{\text{decel}} \le a_{\text{decel}} = 1.20\,\text{m/s}^2$$
$$\left|\frac{d\omega_i}{dt}\right| \le \alpha_{\text{max}} = 1.50\,\text{rad/s}^2$$

