## 4. Rolling-Horizon Collision Resolution (RHCR) 4D Spatio-Temporal Planning

### 4.1 4D State Space & Graph Formulation
The configuration space is discretized into spatio-temporal nodes:
$$\mathbf{s} = (i, j, \theta, k) \in \mathcal{C}_{4D} = \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z} \times \Theta \times \mathbb{N}$$
where $(i, j)$ is the grid cell, $\theta \in \{0, \frac{\pi}{2}, \pi, \frac{3\pi}{2}\}$ represents discrete orientation, and $k$ represents discrete timestep $t = k \cdot \Delta t$.

### 4.2 Spatio-Temporal A* Cost Formulation
The path search evaluates:
$$f(n) = g(n) + h(n)$$

#### Path Cost $g(n)$
$$g(n) = g(\text{parent}) + \Delta g(n)$$
$$\Delta g(n) = \Delta t_{\text{step}} + \alpha_{\text{rot}} \cdot |\Delta \theta| + \beta_{\text{wait}} \cdot \mathbb{I}_{\text{wait}}$$
where:
- $\Delta t_{\text{step}} = 1.0$ (uniform grid step cost)
- $\alpha_{\text{rot}} = 0.20$ (turn penalty discouraging excessive pivoting)
- $\beta_{\text{wait}} = 1.50$ (wait penalty discouraging indefinite stopping)

#### Admissible Heuristic $h(n)$
To guarantee admissibility and optimality, $h(n)$ combines Manhattan distance and minimal angular deflection:
$$h(n) = \frac{\|(i_n, j_n) - (i_{\text{goal}}, j_{\text{goal}})\|_1 \cdot \delta_{\text{grid}}}{v_{\text{max}}} + \alpha_{\text{rot}} \cdot \min\left(|\theta_n - \theta_{\text{goal}}|, \, 2\pi - |\theta_n - \theta_{\text{goal}}|\right)$$

### 4.3 Horizon Truncation & Prefix Execution
Given full path $\Pi_{\text{full}} = (\mathbf{x}_0, \mathbf{x}_1, \dots, \mathbf{x}_{K})$ computed to the active subgoal:
1. **Planning Horizon Lookahead ($h = 10$ steps $\equiv 5.0\,\text{s}$)**:
   $$\Pi_{\text{horizon}} = \Pi_{\text{full}}[0 : \min(K, h+1)]$$
2. **Execution Window Prefix ($w = 4$ steps $\equiv 2.0\,\text{s}$)**:
   $$\Pi_{\text{exec}} = \Pi_{\text{full}}[0 : \min(K, w+1)]$$

The differential-drive controller executes only $\Pi_{\text{exec}}$. When $w$ steps are exhausted, the robot replans.

### 4.4 Replanning Trigger Conditions
Replanning is triggered if and only if:
$$\text{Trigger} \iff \begin{cases} 
\|\mathbf{x}_{\text{robot}} - \mathbf{x}_{\text{subgoal}}\|_2 \le \epsilon_{\text{goal}} = 0.35\,\text{m} & \text{(Subgoal Arrived)} \\ 
\text{steps\_executed} \ge w = 4 & \text{(Window Exhausted)} \\ 
\text{active\_waypoint\_idx} \ge |\Pi_{\text{exec}}| & \text{(Prefix Completed)} \\ 
t - t_{\text{last\_progress}} > 3.0\,\text{s} & \text{(Progress Timeout)} 
\end{cases}$$

