## 7. Wait-For-Graph (WFG) Deadlock Detection & Deterministic Recovery

In multi-robot warehouse intersections and chokepoints, cyclic waiting dependencies can form (Robot $A$ waits for $B$, $B$ waits for $C$, and $C$ waits for $A$).

### 7.1 Directed Graph Representation
The fleet state is represented as a directed graph $G = (V, E)$:
- **Vertices** $V = \{\text{amr}_0, \text{amr}_1, \dots, \text{amr}_{N-1}\}$.
- **Directed Edges** $(u \to v) \in E \iff$ Robot $u$ is waiting for cell $C$ currently occupied or reserved by Robot $v$.

### 7.2 Tarjan's Strongly Connected Components (SCC) Cycle Detection
Evaluated every $1.0\,\text{s}$ across all active reservations:
- Each vertex $u$ maintains discovery index $\text{dfn}[u]$ and lowest reachable index $\text{low}[u]$:
  $$\text{low}[u] = \min \begin{cases} \text{dfn}[u] \\ \text{dfn}[w], & (u, w) \in E \land w \in \text{stack} \\ \text{low}[w], & (u, w) \in E \land w \notin \text{stack} \end{cases}$$
- **Deadlock Condition**: A deadlock exists if any strongly connected component contains two or more vertices:
  $$\exists \text{SCC}_k \subset V \quad \text{s.t.} \quad |\text{SCC}_k| \ge 2$$

### 7.3 Deterministic Evading Robot Election
When cycle $\mathcal{C} = \{r_1, r_2, \dots, r_k\}$ is detected, the evading robot $r^*$ is selected deterministically:
$$r^* = \arg\max_{r \in \mathcal{C}} \text{NumericID}(r) \quad \text{subject to} \quad \mathcal{P}_r = \min_{u \in \mathcal{C}} \mathcal{P}_u$$
The lowest-priority robot (breaking ties with highest numeric robot ID) is elected.

### 7.4 Evasion Maneuver Kinematics
Robot $r^*$ immediately:
1. Relinquishes all active reservations in $\Pi_{\text{exec}}$.
2. Commands reverse linear velocity $v = -0.25\,\text{m/s}$ for distance $d_{\text{retreat}} = 1.50\,\text{m}$ along its reverse heading $-\theta$.
3. Backs into the nearest warehouse passing alcove or charging bay:
   $$\mathbf{x}_{\text{evade}} = \mathbf{x}_{r^*} - 1.50 \begin{bmatrix} \cos\theta_{r^*} \\ \sin\theta_{r^*} \end{bmatrix}$$
4. Re-enters the planning state after a dwell pause of $\tau_{\text{yield}} = 3.0\,\text{s}$.

