## 8. Level 1 Reactive LiDAR Safety Controller (Absolute Authority)

The Reactive LiDAR Safety Controller sits at the lowest level of the autonomy architecture and holds **absolute preemption authority** over all higher-level software commands.

### 8.1 10 Hz Independent Execution Loop
The controller runs on an isolated $10\,\text{Hz}$ ROS 2 timer ($100\,\text{ms}$ period) directly reading raw `sensor_msgs/msg/LaserScan` messages:
$$\mathcal{S} = \left\{ (r_k, \phi_k) \mid k = 1, \dots, K \right\}$$
where $r_k$ is the measured distance and $\phi_k$ is the beam bearing relative to the robot's forward heading ($x$-axis).

### 8.2 Forward Arc Obstacle Filtering
Measurements are filtered to evaluate the forward collision cone:
$$\phi_k \in \left[ -\frac{\theta_{\text{fov}}}{2}, \, +\frac{\theta_{\text{fov}}}{2} \right], \quad \theta_{\text{fov}} = 90^\circ = \frac{\pi}{2}\,\text{rad}$$
The minimum forward obstacle distance is:
$$d_{\text{min}} = \min \left\{ r_k \mid r_k > r_{\text{min\_valid}} \land |\phi_k| \le \frac{\pi}{4} \right\}$$

### 8.3 Piecewise Linear Braking & Emergency Stop Formula
Let $v_{\text{plan}}$ and $\omega_{\text{plan}}$ be the commands requested by RHCR. The commanded velocities $(v_{\text{cmd}}, \omega_{\text{cmd}})$ transmitted to the wheel drivers are:

$$v_{\text{cmd}} = \begin{cases} 
0.00 & \text{if } d_{\text{min}} \le d_{\text{crit}} = 0.35\,\text{m} \quad \text{\bf (EMERGENCY STOP)} \\ 
v_{\text{plan}} \cdot \left(\frac{d_{\text{min}} - d_{\text{crit}}}{d_{\text{warn}} - d_{\text{crit}}}\right) & \text{if } d_{\text{crit}} < d_{\text{min}} \le d_{\text{warn}} = 0.80\,\text{m} \quad \text{\bf (PROPORTIONAL BRAKE)} \\ 
v_{\text{plan}} & \text{if } d_{\text{min}} > d_{\text{warn}} = 0.80\,\text{m} \quad \text{\bf (CLEAR)} 
\end{cases}$$

$$\omega_{\text{cmd}} = \begin{cases} 
0.00 & \text{if } d_{\text{min}} \le d_{\text{crit}} = 0.35\,\text{m} \\ 
\omega_{\text{plan}} \cdot \left(\frac{d_{\text{min}} - d_{\text{crit}}}{d_{\text{warn}} - d_{\text{crit}}}\right) & \text{if } d_{\text{crit}} < d_{\text{min}} \le d_{\text{warn}} \\ 
\omega_{\text{plan}} & \text{if } d_{\text{min}} > d_{\text{warn}} 
\end{cases}$$

### 8.4 Independence Invariant
The safety braking loop is:
- Completely decoupled from A* planning threads.
- Completely decoupled from ROS 2 DDS network connectivity.
- Completely decoupled from CBBA auction convergence states.
- Guaranteed to stop the robot within $d_{\text{stop}} \le \frac{v_{\text{max}}^2}{2 a_{\text{decel}}} = \frac{1.0}{2(1.2)} \approx 0.42\,\text{m}$, preventing physical contact in all evaluated Gazebo scenarios.

