## 10. Adaptive Compute Policy Engine: Dynamic Hysteresis & Throttling

The `AdaptiveComputePolicy` runs as an onboard governor that monitors CPU load, network health, and spatial contention to modulate planning parameters dynamically.

### 10.1 Discrete Compute Modes & Parameters
Three operational modes are defined:

$$\begin{array}{|l|c|c|c|c|c|}
\hline
\text{\bf Mode} & f_{\text{replan}} \text{ (Hz)} & \text{Horizon } h & \text{Window } w & f_{\text{cbba}} \text{ (Hz)} & \text{Budget } \tau_{\text{plan}} \text{ (ms)} \\
\hline
\text{\bf LOW} & 1.0 & 6 & 6 & 2.0 & 20.0 \\
\text{\bf NORMAL} & 2.0 & 10 & 4 & 5.0 & 50.0 \\
\text{\bf HIGH} & 4.0 & 14 & 2 & 10.0 & 100.0 \\
\hline
\end{array}$$

### 10.2 Host Telemetry Smoothing
CPU utilization is sampled via `psutil` and smoothed via exponential moving average:
$$\bar{u}_{\text{CPU}}(t) = \alpha_{\text{smooth}} \cdot u_{\text{CPU}}(t) + (1 - \alpha_{\text{smooth}}) \cdot \bar{u}_{\text{CPU}}(t-1), \quad \alpha_{\text{smooth}} = 0.30$$

### 10.3 Priority-Ordered Evaluation State Machine
Transitions evaluate signals in strict order of severity:
1. **Network Degradation (Triggers LOW)**:
   $$\bar{t}_{\text{stale}} \ge 1.50\,\text{s} \quad \lor \quad p_{\text{loss}} \ge 0.15 \quad \lor \quad \tau_{\text{plan}} \ge 15.0\,\text{ms}$$
2. **Compute Resource Pressure (Triggers LOW)**:
   $$\bar{u}_{\text{CPU}}(t) \ge 85.0\%$$
3. **Recovery to NORMAL (from LOW)**:
   $$\bar{t}_{\text{stale}} \le 0.80\,\text{s} \quad \land \quad p_{\text{loss}} \le 0.05 \quad \land \quad \bar{u}_{\text{CPU}}(t) \le 65.0\%$$
4. **Traffic Contention (Triggers HIGH from NORMAL)**:
   $$N_{\text{conflicts\_in\_window}} \ge 2 \quad \land \quad \bar{u}_{\text{CPU}}(t) < 70.0\%$$
5. **Recovery to NORMAL (from HIGH)**:
   $$N_{\text{conflicts\_in\_window}} == 0 \quad \lor \quad \bar{u}_{\text{CPU}}(t) \ge 75.0\%$$

### 10.4 Anti-Oscillation Safeguards
To prevent mode chatter:
1. **Minimum Dwell Time**:
   $$t_{\text{now}} - t_{\text{last\_transition}} \ge T_{\text{dwell}} = 3.00\,\text{s}$$
2. **Consecutive Confirmation Samples**:
   A candidate mode transition is committed only after $K = 3$ consecutive affirmative evaluation cycles.
3. **Fail-Safe Fallback**:
   If telemetry becomes null or times out ($t_{\text{now}} - t_{\text{telemetry}} > 5.0\,\text{s}$), the policy falls back to `NORMAL`.

